course: dictionary
lesson: 10204
title: Tipi: a home on the Plains
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tipi is a tent. Its shape is a cone, which means it is round at the bottom and comes to a point at the top. Read the sentence: «Feathered headdresses and tipis belonged to some Plains peoples, not to all Native Americans.» The word some is a clue. It means only a part of a group, not every one.
explain: Now read the second sentence: «On the Great Plains nations such as the Lakota followed huge herds of bison, using almost every part for food, clothing, tools and tipi covers.» Bison are large animals, also called buffalo. The Lakota followed the herds, so they moved from place to place, and a tipi was easy to take down and carry.
explain: Notice the phrases too. You can put up a tipi, which means you build it, and you can be inside the tipi. Tipi covers are the skins or cloth that wrap around the poles. When you read about a tipi in history, ask yourself which people used it and why.
fact: A tipi is a cone-shaped tent.
fact: A tipi is made of animal skins or cloth stretched over long wooden poles.
fact: Tipi can also be spelled tepee or teepee.
fact: Tipis were traditionally used by some Native American peoples of the Great Plains, such as the Lakota.
fact: Tipis are also used today at festivals and camps.
exercise: What is a tipi? | *A cone-shaped tent made of animal skins or cloth over long wooden poles | A kind of hat worn at festivals | A wooden house with a flat roof | A large herd of bison
exercise: «Feathered headdresses and tipis belonged to some Plains peoples, not to all Native Americans.» What does the word some tell you? | Everyone, all of them together | *Only a part of the group, not every one | Nobody at all | Only the children
exercise: Which people followed huge herds of bison across the Great Plains? | *The Lakota | The Vikings | The ancient Egyptians | The Romans
test: Which of these is another spelling of tipi? | tapee | topping | tipper | *tepee
test: According to the sentence, what did the Lakota use bison for? | Building railways | *Food, clothing, tools and tipi covers | Pulling ploughs | Making paper
exam: Why does the sentence say «some Plains peoples, not all Native Americans»? | Because all Native Americans lived in tipis | Because the Plains were covered by water | *Because only some peoples of the Plains used feathered headdresses and tipis | Because tipis were only built by the Spanish
